# verify-ticks — verify checked-off items against real communications

🔴🔴 **MANUAL ONLY. Never run automatically.** This skill runs ONLY when the operator explicitly asks — trigger phrases: "verify ticks", "check my checkboxes", "did I actually do those", "проверь отмеченное". Do NOT run it on every tick, NOT on a schedule, NOT inside the morning briefing.

## Why

On the dashboard, the operator ticks a checkbox = "I did this, stop reminding me." But humans mis-remember — they think they replied / called / paid, and in reality they didn't (or it isn't reflected anywhere). This skill applies the never-imagine-always-verify rule to the operator's *own* checkmarks: for every checked item, go to the REAL communications (all connected mail accounts + chat read-MCPs) and either confirm it with evidence, or say honestly "no evidence found — you may not have done it."

The point is trust calibration, not policing: a ⚠️ verdict is a calm "you ticked this but I can't find proof — double-check?", never an accusation.

## Steps

### 1. Pull the checked items

Read `<workspace>/state/dashboard/dashboard-closed.json` (produced by the dashboard's **export state** button; see `dashboard/README.md`). It lists every closed `card_id` with its first-checked timestamp.

Recover each item's text from the current `dashboard/index.html`: for each `card_id`, find `data-card-id="<id>"` and take the adjacent card/line text (title + body). `card_id`s that no longer exist in `index.html` (the item aged out of the source markdown) — **skip**.

Skip items already verified: read `<workspace>/state/dashboard/tick-verifications.json` (card_id → {verdict, verified_at}). If a verdict exists and the item's checked-at timestamp hasn't changed, don't re-verify (unless the operator says "re-check everything").

### 2. For each item — define what "done" means

From the item text, work out the action + counterparty + channel: "call the packaging vendor back" → was there a call/message to that vendor; "send the tracking numbers to the 3PL" → did an email/chat message with tracking numbers go out; "pay the counsel invoice" → is there a payment confirmation or a receipt reply; "reply to X" → is there an outbound message to X. Some items are not verifiable from communications at all (personal: "pack the suitcase", "sign on the portal") → mark them ℹ️ not-verifiable; do not guess.

### 3. Launch one verifier agent per verifiable item (in parallel)

For each item, a separate subagent (worker) with this brief:

- Given: the item text + counterparty + what "done" means.
- Scan: all connected mail accounts (`in:sent` AND inbox, by counterparty/topic, `newer_than:21d`) + chat read-MCPs (search / messages-with by counterparty, including relevant group chats).
- 🔴 Only REAL messages count as evidence — quote + date + channel. Invent nothing. Never web-search private people or deals.
- Return a verdict: **✅ VERIFIED** (evidence: "<quote>" — <channel>, <date>) / **⚠️ NO EVIDENCE** (searched X, Y — found nothing; possibly not done or not reflected) / **ℹ️ N/A** (not verifiable from communications).

Launch the agents together (parallel), not one at a time.

### 4. Report to the operator (inline in chat, or to the channel the trigger came from)

Per item: icon + short verdict + evidence (for ✅) / what was searched (for ⚠️). Format:

```
Checked-item verification (N items):
✅ Vendor-A callback — chat "spoke, all good" <date>
✅ Counsel invoice — "Payment received" <date> (inbox)
⚠️ 3PL tracking numbers — no outbound message with the numbers found (their last message to you is <date>, no reply from you). Sure you sent it?
ℹ️ Portal signature — personal, not verifiable from communications.
```

The ⚠️ items are the whole point: calmly surface "ticked but unproven — worth a re-check", without accusation.

### 5. Persist the result

Update `<workspace>/state/dashboard/tick-verifications.json`: `{card_id: {verdict, evidence, verified_at}}`. This (a) prevents re-verification, (b) lets the morning-briefing skill optionally mark ⚠️-verdict items as "ticked-but-unverified" and gently resurface them. The morning briefing reads this file optionally; only verify-ticks writes it.

## Hard rules

- MANUAL ONLY (see top). Auto-running this = a bug.
- Only the operator's own communications (mail / chat MCPs). No web-searching private people or deals.
- Evidence = a real quote from a real message. No message → ⚠️, NOT ✅. Never "probably did it".
- 2+ agents: each item is verified by a subagent; for borderline calls ("not sure it's the same thread") — a second independent pass before saying ✅.
- This skill only READS the closed state + index.html. It never modifies the dashboard or its sync layer.
